From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 19:46:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server, ntdll, kernelbase: Keep a process's mitigation
 policies in the server, and those it is created with.

A process's policies were kept in its own ntdll, so another process
asking saw only the defaults, and the policies a process was created
with (PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_MITIGATION_POLICY, CHILD_PROCESS_POLICY)
were ignored with a FIXME.  The server now keeps those that were set;
the defaults still come from ntdll, which gains SEH overwrite
protection, and pointer authentication is ARM64's only.

The creation options become policies as Windows 11 turns them into
them (tools/startupgapsprobe misc, misc3: 26 options measured): each
two-bit option on, off or its third choice, high entropy ASLR going
with bottom-up ASLR, shadow stacks with context IP validation.  A
restricted child may not create processes (ERROR_CHILD_PROCESS_BLOCKED);
the child process policy takes a DWORD only.  winbase.h gets the
PROCESS_CREATION_* constants.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

